{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"370f40dc-cb51-4c85-bdd6-b3cb194776f2","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have resolved the caching issue where saving memory facts evicted the static instructions.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Split System Prompt into Two Cached Segments ([`build_system`](file:///tmp/h-ErIukq/bot.py#L130-L138) in [bot.py](file:///tmp/h-ErIukq/bot.py))**:\n   - **Segment 1 (Static instructions)**: Kept invariant coaching rules (`INSTRUCTIONS`) with its own `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` marker. Because Anthropic prompt caching works as a prefix hash, this block remains hot across all athletes, requests, and tool rounds.\n   - **Segment 2 (Volatile context tail)**: Placed dynamic athlete context (`athlete_context(a, today)`, containing date, profile, zones, goal, facts, and language) with a second `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` marker. When `save_fact` appends a new fact, only this ~250–300 token tail is invalidated and recreated rather than the entire ~1000+ token system prompt.\n\n2. **Documentation ([ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-ErIukq/ANSWER.md))**:\n   - Detailed the code changes and analyzed which parts of the colleague's note applied (two `cache_control` markers and prefix hash mechanics) versus which did not apply or were already satisfied (tool filtering, avoiding per-message top-N fact selection, and usage metric logging).\n","duration_seconds":63.104748,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":105979,"output_tokens":1846,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":159754,"total_tokens":107825}}}
